1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Hairstyling was very important to victorian women.
发型对维多利亚时代的女性很重要。

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:09,320
When deciding what style I wanted to do I referred to the book and chose one of the illustrations and then I also found.
决定要做什么发型时，我查阅了那本书，选了一幅插图，然后还找到了……

3
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:17,270
Another image online and decided to do a mixture between the two.
……另一张网上的图片，决定把两者结合起来。

4
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:22,160
I knew that I would need a center part and some hair products to get me started.
我知道要先分一个中分，还得用些美发产品来开始。

5
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:31,670
And in the victorian era hair oils were something between a conditioner um and like a lotion for frizz control.
维多利亚时代的发油有点介于护发素和控制毛躁的乳液之间。

6
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:40,230
I used some hair oil to prep my hair before styling.
我在造型前先用一点发油打底、整理头发。

7
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:44,789
And then I started the style by creating two small braids in the front.
然后我从前面编两条小辫子，开始做这个发型。

8
00:00:44,799 --> 00:00:54,070
And these were the ones that will wrap around and under my hair to connect around the bun in the back afterwards.
之后这两条辫子会绕过去、从头发下面穿过，接到后面的发髻周围。

9
00:00:54,080 --> 00:00:59,840
Then I gathered my hair together in the pictures it's really really sleek and that's what I was going for.
然后我把头发拢在一起。图片里的头发非常平顺，而这正是我想达到的效果。

10
00:00:59,840 --> 00:01:07,280
So then I created a regular braid I noticed that one of the pictures the bun was sitting really low on her head.
接着我编了一条普通辫子。我注意到其中一张图里的发髻位置很低。

11
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:09,240
And so that's how I tried to do mine.
所以我也试着把自己的发髻做成那样。

12
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:13,960
I just wrapped the braid around and pinned it into place with a handful of bobby pins.
我把辫子绕起来，再用一把发夹把它固定住。

13
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:25,350
And also some help from jared.
Jared 也帮了些忙。

14
00:01:25,360 --> 00:01:29,990
Looking back I wish I would have chosen a hairstyle later in the victorian era.
回头看，我真希望选的是维多利亚时代较晚期的发型。

15
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,040
As I think this one did not suit my face type at all.
因为我觉得这个发型一点也不适合我的脸型。

16
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:39,670
I know queen victoria also liked this detailing of having the braids go around the ears on the side.
我知道维多利亚女王也喜欢这种细节，也就是让辫子绕过两侧的耳朵。

17
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:43,799
But it is just not for me I had fun creating it though.
但这真的不适合我。不过做的过程还是挺开心的。

18
00:01:43,799 --> 00:01:48,640
And after it was all put together I just added some pomade to hide my bangs.
整体弄好后，我加了一点发蜡，把刘海藏起来。

19
00:01:48,640 --> 00:02:01,550
Since they weren't really part of this hairstyle so I didn't want to include them.
因为这个发型原本没有刘海，所以我不想把刘海放进去。

20
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:08,269
The next step of a victorian woman's morning routine required her to decide whether she would wear makeup or not.
维多利亚时代女性晨间流程的下一步，是决定要不要化妆。

21
00:02:08,279 --> 00:02:14,360
Queen victoria did not include makeup as she viewed the practice as vulgar and impolite.
维多利亚女王不把化妆纳入其中，因为她认为这种做法粗俗、不够得体。

22
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:18,280
Which definitely influenced how women at the time also viewed makeup.
这当然也影响了当时女性看待化妆的方式。

23
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:25,560
The girls own paper published an article stating that pimples could be prevented by a light diet.
《女孩自己的报纸》刊过一篇文章，声称清淡饮食能预防青春痘。

24
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:29,240
And that a daily walk provided all the colors the cheeks needed.
还声称每天散步就能让面颊拥有所需的全部红润色泽。

25
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:32,200
And that getting up at dawn made the lips bright and red.
并声称黎明起床会让嘴唇鲜红明亮。

26
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:35,799
And the desire of pleasing will add fire to a woman's eyes.
而想要取悦别人的心意会让女性的眼睛增添光彩。

27
00:02:35,799 --> 00:02:42,070
And while other victorian women were less passionate about the subject they nonetheless agreed with this article in principle.
其他维多利亚时代女性虽然对这话题没那么热衷，但在原则上还是赞同这篇文章。

28
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:55,750
And then the final touch before embarking on a proper day was the application of perfume.
开始正式一天之前，最后一步是喷香水。

29
00:02:55,760 --> 00:03:02,880
A common victorian breakfast consisted of porridge bacon and possibly some cold meats cheeses and breads.
常见的维多利亚式早餐有粥、培根，可能还包括一些冷肉、奶酪和面包。

30
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:09,110
And the time at which breakfast was eaten and the foods included very much differed based on class.
吃早餐的时间、早餐里的食物，都因社会阶层而有很大差别。

31
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:15,560
Ruth goodman explained that before tea was britain's traditional drink many people actually drink beer with their breakfast.
Ruth Goodman 解释说，在茶成为英国的传统饮品以前，很多人早餐其实会喝啤酒。

32
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:23,000
It provided not only valuable calories but a range of minerals and vitamins that were otherwise lacking in most people's diets.
它不仅提供有价值的热量，还提供大多数人饮食里原先缺少的多种矿物质和维生素。

33
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,360
But eventually tea and coffee and cocoa became more popular.
但后来茶、咖啡和可可更流行了。

34
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:32,680
And hot cocoa is actually viewed as a healthy and energy giving drink that many people drank with their breakfast.
热可可实际上被看作一种健康、能提供能量的饮料，很多人会配早餐喝。

35
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:48,520
The final step in this routine is morning exercise in the 1860 s.
这套流程的最后一步是晨间运动。在十九世纪六十年代。

36
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:56,120
Medical professionals recommended walking lots of walking not athletic hill walking or anything too strenuous.
医疗人员当时推荐走路，多多走路；不是运动式爬山，也不是过于费力的活动。

37
00:03:56,120 --> 00:04:03,680
But daily hour long walks especially to be taken in the morning when the body was clean and fresh.
而是每天走一小时，尤其在早晨，身体刚洗净、清爽的时候去。

38
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:10,320
It was a free form of exercise requiring no special clothes equipment or location.
这是一种免费的运动，不需要特别的衣服、设备或地点。

39
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:15,320
Anyone could walk around and enjoy the open air the richest to the poorest.
无论最富有还是最贫穷的人，都可以四处走走，享受户外空气。

40
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:19,320
And I decided to bring along a few of my favorite victorian novels.
我决定带上几本自己最喜欢的维多利亚时代小说。

41
00:04:19,320 --> 00:04:24,000
And enjoy the warm sunshine as we finish up with this victorian morning routine.
在温暖的阳光下享受一下，就这样结束这次维多利亚式晨间体验。
